      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-240628",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/6a/6aa5c2e19ad523bcd4d4e44526f3286f2915b96d87b8fa7e2625312ba8ccf8a1.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, the angles $\u2220BAE$ and $\u2220AEF$ are supplementary.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *The lines $BD^(\u27f7)$ and $FG^(\u27f7)$ are parallel.*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $\u2220BAE$ and $\u2220AEF$ are supplementary | Given |\n| 2 | $m\u2220BAE + m\u2220AEF = 180^{\u2218}$ | Definition of supplementary angles |\n| 3 | $m\u2220AEF = 180^{\u2218} - m\u2220BAE$ | Addition principle |\n| 4 | $\u2220CAB$ and $\u2220BAE$ are supplementary | {{field-1}} |\n| 5 | $m\u2220CAB + m\u2220BAE = 180^{\u2218}$ | Definition of supplementary angles |\n| 6 | $m\u2220CAB = 180^{\u2218} - m\u2220BAE$ | Addition principle |\n| 7 | $m\u2220CAB = m\u2220AEF$ | Transitive property of equality |\n| 8 | $\u2220CAB\u2245\u2220AEF$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 9 | $BD^(\u27f7)$ and $FG^(\u27f7)$ are parallel lines | {{field-3}} |"
    },
